---
const items = [
  {
    q: 'Why Lit Web Components and not React, Vue or Svelte?',
    a: 'Lit compiles to standard Web Components, which the browser runs natively. The runtime is ~38 KB gz (engine + Lit + marked), against ~50 KB for React plus ReactDOM, and it needs no build step on your side. A deck stays a folder. Open it in 2031, it still runs.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need to know Lit to write a deck?',
    a: 'No. You write HTML tags. Lit is what built the components under the hood. What you touch is plain HTML and CSS custom properties. No decorators, no template literals, no extending classes.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I print my deck to PDF?',
    a: 'Yes, from the browser. Chromium with print-backgrounds on gives the cleanest result. There is no separate CLI. Slides are plain HTML, so the browser print pipeline handles it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a presenter mode with notes?',
    a: 'Yes. Wrap notes in <code>&lt;deck-notes&gt;</code> inside any slide, then press P during the talk. A popup opens with the current and next slide, the notes, a timer and a slide counter. Sync runs over BroadcastChannel. No network call.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I theme a deck for my brand?',
    a: 'Copy <code>themes/rikiki.css</code>, change the values, link it instead of the default. ~140 CSS custom properties, in two layers (palette, then semantic). For a one-off, override the <code>--deck-*-*</code> tokens inline on the element.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What if I want an animation that is not in the box?',
    a: 'Drop a <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> inside any slide and run whatever JS you like. The slide is just an HTML host. Most of the time the four built-in transitions (slide, fade, zoom, flip) cover it. For one-off effects, GSAP and friends are a script tag away.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why also pitch carousels?',
    a: 'Because <code>autoplay loop swipe</code> on <code>&lt;deck-root&gt;</code> turns the same engine into a touch-friendly carousel. Same components, same theming, same ~38 KB initial load. The dual use falls out of building on web standards.',
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="faq">
  <div class="inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
    <h2>Common questions</h2>

    <div class="list">
      {items.map((it) => (
        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q">{it.q}</span>
            <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="a" set:html={it.a}></div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    background: var(--rik-surface-raised);
    padding: var(--rik-space-7) var(--rik-space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default);
  }
  .inner { max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--rik-accent);
    color: var(--rik-accent__on);
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: var(--rik-radius-pill);
    font: 700 var(--rik-font-size-xs)/1 var(--rik-font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: var(--rik-space-3);
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--rik-font-display);
    font-size: var(--rik-font-size-mega);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0 0 var(--rik-space-5);
  }
  .list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default);
    padding: var(--rik-space-3) 0;
  }
  details:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default); }
  summary {
    display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--rik-space-3);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    padding: var(--rik-space-2) 0;
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    font-family: var(--rik-font-display);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    line-height: 1.35;
    transition: color var(--rik-motion-fast) var(--rik-motion__ease-out);
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary:hover { color: var(--rik-accent--strong); }
  .chev {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 28px; height: 28px;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default);
    border-radius: 50%;
    color: var(--rik-text-default--faint);
    font: 700 1.1rem/1 var(--rik-font-mono);
    transition: transform var(--rik-motion-base) var(--rik-motion__ease-out),
                background var(--rik-motion-fast) var(--rik-motion__ease-out),
                color var(--rik-motion-fast) var(--rik-motion__ease-out);
  }
  details[open] .chev {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    background: var(--rik-accent);
    color: var(--rik-accent__on);
    border-color: var(--rik-accent);
  }
  .a {
    padding: var(--rik-space-2) 0 var(--rik-space-2);
    color: var(--rik-text-default--muted);
    font-size: var(--rik-font-size-body);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .a :global(code) {
    font-family: var(--rik-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--rik-surface-tint);
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
</style>
